# Currencies

Money carries its currency: a symbol before the number or a code after it.

[€450]:hotel
[700 MXN]:fee
[$1,200]:flights

[hotel_usd] := to(hotel, USD)
[fee_usd] := to(fee, USD)
[trip] := flights + hotel_usd + fee_usd

The hotel is [hotel], about [hotel_usd]; the trip totals [trip].
One euro is [rate(EUR, USD)] dollars.

<!-- Rates come from the lookup cache: run jot refresh or use the Refresh lookups lens.
Try: write flights + hotel to see why mixing currencies is an error. -->
